# Modelfile for the local bill-text embedding model.
#
# Wraps the Ollama-published `qwen3-embedding:0.6b` (≈ 0.5 GB on disk) with parameters tuned for our hardware
# profile (single GPU, 8 GB VRAM) and our workload profile (long bill texts, batched chunk embedding). The
# resulting tuned variant is registered as `bill-text-embedding` (generic name — the tag stays stable as the
# underlying base model is swapped over time, so the data-ingestion env-var contract `OLLAMA_MODEL_NAME` does
# not move with each tuning change).
#
# Why 0.6B instead of 4B (the previous baseline):
#   - 4B (≈ 2.5 GB on disk, ≈ 6 GB VRAM resident) saturated the GPU at ~10-chunk batches because the model
#     itself ate most of the available VRAM, leaving little room for KV cache + activations + larger batches.
#   - 0.6B (≈ 0.5 GB on disk, ≈ 1 GB VRAM resident) frees ~5 GB for KV cache and activations on the same
#     8 GB card, lifting the GPU-saturation batch size to ~50. That's a ~5× throughput multiplier for the
#     batch-friendly path (`/api/embed` with an array of inputs) at minimal retrieval-quality cost: the qwen3
#     family uses Matryoshka representation learning and the 0.6B's native 1024-dim output (vs 1536 for 4B,
#     2560 for 8B) is a truncated MRL slice, not a capability loss. Bill-text similarity benchmarks remain
#     within noise.
#   - The dim swap requires a coordinated `raw_bill_text.embedding` schema migration (db-migrations 028,
#     vector(1536) → vector(1024)) shipped in lockstep with this Modelfile change.
#
# Why the parameters:
#   - num_ctx 16384: doubled from the 8192 baseline because legislative text is unusually dense
#     (citations, statute references, formal definitions) and tokenizes at well below 4 char/token in many
#     cases. Empirically, our 12000-char chunks were exceeding 8192 tokens often enough to trigger Ollama's
#     silent input-truncation path — Ollama logs INFO `"input length exceeds the context length"` and
#     returns an embedding of just the first 8192 tokens, which our pipeline cannot detect (HTTP 200,
#     valid-shape vector returned). 178 truncation events surfaced in ~1 hour of local ingestion before we
#     bumped this. 16384 gives ~2× headroom over the worst-case observed token count and still fits the 0.6B
#     model's KV-cache budget on an 8 GB card with room to spare.
#   - num_batch 512: tokens per forward-pass batch on prompt evaluation. Default is 128. 512 better
#     utilizes the GPU's tensor cores on long-input embed workloads.
#   - num_gpu 99: force ALL transformer layers to GPU (Ollama's "as many as possible" sentinel). With 0.6B
#     this is trivially satisfied — the model fits with room to spare.

FROM qwen3-embedding:0.6b

PARAMETER num_ctx 16384
PARAMETER num_batch 512
PARAMETER num_gpu 99
